070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399145 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear differential equations given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x(t).\n$$\n\nGiven that the solution to the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}t{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186399145 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1bd476b7-be13-5d1b-9c4d-aad2517551db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399145 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince $A$ is lower-triangular, the repeated eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-1$ (of multiplicity two).\nFor this eigenvalue, we get \n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n$v=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSince we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda $ and only one linearly independent eigenvector $v$, the solution of the system of differential equations is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nTo find $w,$ we solve the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-\\lambda I)w & =v \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-1+1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1+1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equality allows us to form the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0{w}_{1}+0{w}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 4{w}_{1}+0{w}_{2} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n{w}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe variable ${w}_{2}$ is a free variable. Setting ${w}_{2}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nw=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}t{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, we see that $a=0,b=\\frac{1}{4},$ and $a+b=\\frac{1}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186399146 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399146 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399146 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399146 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399146 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399146 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399146 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399146 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186399148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399146 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "162ccab1-6783-5e36-870b-96a5c241f52b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399147 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{3}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399147 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399147 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eba8c50d-8cd6-567a-b472-75707ce03343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399148 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399148 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399148 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5e646bbf-5ae7-5023-a552-e22b215170d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399149 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399149 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399149 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6f01c0dd-442a-5b90-8